# The area diagram: a whole split by proportion, so area is probability. Strips d[i]; by= splits each again (d[i][j]).
title "Rain and umbrellas"
mark d area parts=[3,7] labels=["rain (30%)","dry (70%)"] colors=[blue,-] label="all days"
Say: "Three days in ten it rains."
mark d by=[[8,2],[1,9]] bylabels=["umbrella","none","umbrella","none"] bycolors=[yellow,-,yellow,-]
Say: "On rainy days, eight in ten people carry an umbrella; on dry days, one in ten."
Say: "So rain |both|and an umbrella is a quarter of all days."
@both mark u enclose of=d[0][0] label="0.3 × 0.8 = 0.24"
